From 5d0eafdd8d938585f7cd731e3cf84f472bc8d50a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 15:10:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] rtc_base: enumerate networks from AROSTCP snapshots
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: WebRTC built and called getifaddrs on every POSIX target, but AROS provides neither ifaddrs.h nor that enumeration API. A fake compatibility struct would duplicate native interface policy and leak AROS headers into WebRTC.

FIX_REASON: Exclude the ifaddrs converter on AROS and construct WebRTC Network objects from Chromium's normalized AROSTCP snapshot, preserving prefixes, IPv6 scope, loopback classification, VPN overrides, ignore policy, and network-monitor metadata.

SCOPE: rtc_base network implementation/header and GN dependency selection.

VALIDATION: focused network.o compiles after the full graph failed on ifaddrs_converter.o; the Chromium adapter object compiles independently.

RISK: medium; interface change notification still uses the provisional polling/event path and requires runtime validation.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
